# Security baseline (2026-09-04). The site is static with no user input, no
# third-party scripts and no fetches, so every source is 'self'. Script is
# self-only since 2026-09-07, when the 27 KB of inline page script moved to
# sections.js. Style elements are self-only from the same day, when the 37 KB
# inline block in index.html and the four smaller ones moved to per-page
# stylesheets and radars.js stopped appending a <style> of its own; the five
# inline style="" attributes in bio, sources and for-llms stay (the scripts set
# element.style through the CSSOM, which CSP never gates), so style-src-attr
# keeps 'unsafe-inline' while style-src-elem is 'self'. The
# bare style-src is the fallback for a browser that predates the -elem/-attr
# split (Safari before 15.4) and is 'self' so that fallback is the strict one.
# The guard is `npm run check:csp`, which fails on any inline <script> that is
# not hashed here and on any inline <style> at all. HSTS is set without
# includeSubDomains so no other host under the domain is committed by this file.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; style-src-elem 'self'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/site.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json

# /regulation/* (staged 2026-09-07, unreviewed; see regulation/README.md). The map
# loads Leaflet 1.9.4 from unpkg and Chart.js 4.4.0 from jsDelivr, both pinned with
# subresource integrity in reg-map.html, and map tiles from Carto. Leaflet positions
# panes through the CSSOM and both pages carry inline style attributes, so style-src
# keeps 'unsafe-inline' here. form-action stays 'self' because the lp-interest form
# posts to /regulation/ for Netlify Forms. Everything else is the root baseline. This
# block is the whole header set for the path, so the root CSP is not loosened: a
# request under /regulation/ gets this policy and every other path keeps the root one.
/regulation/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://unpkg.com; style-src-elem 'self' https://unpkg.com; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://unpkg.com https://*.basemaps.cartocdn.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
